-- Issue 134: without --acn-v2 an OCTET / BIT STRING (CONTAINING T) with an embedded length or a fixed size is decoded
-- into a temporary buffer of T's maximum and encoded by T's own function. A site ACN specification that changes the
-- size of the contents (here [size 32] for an 8-bit INTEGER of T) made the region larger than that buffer: the legacy
-- decoders wrote past it on every valid stream. Without --acn-v2 such a specification is rejected; --acn-v2 accepts it
-- (23-CONTAINING/020 round-trips the OCTET STRING forms). No directives: run by v4Tests/scripts/runWireTests.sh with
-- 009_emb.acn, 009_fix.acn, 009_bits.acn (one component with such a specification each: embedded length, fixed size,
-- BIT STRING), 009_bits12.acn (a BIT STRING region 4 bits longer: the same octets, a length range of 13 .. 14 bits for
-- contents of 9 .. 10), 009_emb6.acn (one more bit: 3 .. 4 octets for contents of 2 .. 4, the encoder wrote a length
-- below its range) and 009_same.acn (child specifications that keep the sizes: accepted in both modes).
ACN-WIRE-SITE-SPEC DEFINITIONS AUTOMATIC TAGS ::= BEGIN
    T     ::= SEQUENCE { a INTEGER (0..255), b BOOLEAN OPTIONAL }
    Fx    ::= SEQUENCE { a INTEGER (0..255), b INTEGER (0..255) }
    Emb   ::= SEQUENCE { f OCTET STRING (CONTAINING T), z BOOLEAN }
    Fix   ::= SEQUENCE { g OCTET STRING (CONTAINING Fx), z BOOLEAN }
    Bits  ::= SEQUENCE { h BIT STRING (CONTAINING T), z BOOLEAN }
    T6    ::= SEQUENCE { a INTEGER (0..255), b INTEGER (0..127), c INTEGER (0..1023) OPTIONAL }
    Emb6  ::= SEQUENCE { f OCTET STRING (CONTAINING T6), z BOOLEAN }
END
